flowchart LR
    Start["<b>1. interface enables IPv6</b><br/>joins required multicast groups and prepares link-local state<br/><b>handoff:</b> every IPv6 node needs a usable link-local address<br/><b>state:</b> tentative device IPv6 configuration"]

    LinkLocal["<b>2. link-local + DAD</b><br/>derive fe80:: address and probe for duplicates<br/><b>handoff:</b> no duplicate means control traffic can use the link<br/><b>state:</b> link-local address is preferred or rejected"]

    RA["<b>3. Router Advertisement</b><br/>learn prefixes, lifetimes, default router, A/M/O flags<br/><b>handoff:</b> flags select SLAAC, DHCPv6, or both<br/><b>state:</b> router and prefix policy are known"]

    Addr["<b>4. address configuration</b><br/>SLAAC forms an address, DHCPv6 obtains managed data<br/><b>handoff:</b> each new address must pass DAD before use<br/><b>state:</b> global address and options are installed"]

    Ready["<b>5. NDP-ready interface</b><br/>neighbor discovery resolves next hops and tracks reachability<br/><b>state:</b> IPv6 can send to local-link neighbors and routers"]

    Start --> LinkLocal --> RA --> Addr --> Ready
    LinkLocal -. duplicate .-> Start

    classDef init fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef decision fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef ready fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class Start,RA init
    class LinkLocal,Addr decision
    class Ready ready
